   "subject": "Sample size? Bootstrapping issues, wide variances for D and unrealistic \"p\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Sample sizes:<div><br></div><div>ETTI - Stratified by 2 samples, n1 = 66, n2 = 40</div><div>NOCA - Stratified by 2 samples, n1 = 81, n2 = 18</div><div><br></div><div>-----<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">-----------------------</span></div><div>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I’m using version 6.2 and have\r\nvariable-width line transects. I came up with relatively low sample sizes (in\r\nDISTANCE standards) for each species.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">1. When I try bootstrapping for\r\nEastern Tufted Titmice (ETTI) I am<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">getting a bootstrap warning:\r\nconvergence failure. Does this mean that<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">the bootstrapping variances for\r\n&quot;D&quot; are invalid?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">2. In my Northern Cardinal (NOCA)\r\nanalyses set, My attempts at<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">bootstrapping has always been met with\r\nthe error: “Analysis Engine Terminated Unexpectedly”. Sometimes with an error\r\nsignifying that there may be a problem with input or output files. I have tried\r\ndifferent levels of resampling (e.g. samples vs<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">observations) and different numbers\r\nfrom 199 to 999 and I&#39;m still<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">getting a crash. Is this because of\r\nlow sample size or a program issue?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">3. My &quot;p&quot;, probability of\r\ndetections are concernedly low for conspicuous<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">forest birds, my advisor says that\r\nthey are typically at 0.8/0.9 but I&#39;m<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">seeing 0.2/0.3. Does this mean the modeling\r\nseems to be invalid, or is<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">this just reflecting the reality of\r\nthe sample? Note that there is an<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">interesting potential difference in\r\nobserver &quot;p&quot; between treatments<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">because of the highway noise, but it\r\ndoesn&#39;t show up as significantly<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">different for ETTI or NOCA sets in\r\nmost analyses.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I really appreciate your time,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Best Regards,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Aaron</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(246,246,246)\"><u></u><u></u></span></span></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Mo56uj3MXkoJ",
   "from": "Eric Rexstad",
   "author": "f2122b34f1aa6e95",
   "date": "2014-12-02T10:02:23Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] Sample size? Bootstrapping issues, wide variances for D and unrealistic \"p\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\">\r\n    Aaron:<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    See comments below on your 3 issues:</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>On 01/12/2014 16:55, Aaron Grade wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      \r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">Sample sizes:\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div>ETTI - Stratified by 2 samples, n1 = 66, n2 = 40</div>\r\n        <div>NOCA - Stratified by 2 samples, n1 = 81, n2 = 18</div>\r\n        <div><br>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div>-----<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">-----------------------</span></div>\r\n        <div>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I’m using version\r\n              6.2 and have\r\n              variable-width line transects. I came up with relatively\r\n              low sample sizes (in\r\n              DISTANCE standards) for each species.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">1. When I try\r\n              bootstrapping for\r\n              Eastern Tufted Titmice (ETTI) I am<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">getting a bootstrap\r\n              warning:\r\n              convergence failure. Does this mean that<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">the bootstrapping\r\n              variances for\r\n              &quot;D&quot; are invalid?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\">\r\n    I believe Distance does not use replicates in which there was a\r\n    convergence failure in the variance estimates.  So the number of\r\n    replicates will decrease when there are convergence failures.  You\r\n    can check by looking at the Bootstrap Stats File (described on page\r\n    108 of the Users guide accompanying version 6.2).</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><br>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n        <div>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <br>\r\n              <u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">2. In my Northern\r\n              Cardinal (NOCA)\r\n              analyses set, My attempts at<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">bootstrapping has\r\n              always been met with\r\n              the error: “Analysis Engine Terminated Unexpectedly”.\r\n              Sometimes with an error\r\n              signifying that there may be a problem with input or\r\n              output files. I have tried\r\n              different levels of resampling (e.g. samples vs<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">observations) and\r\n              different numbers\r\n              from 199 to 999 and I&#39;m still<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">getting a crash. Is\r\n              this because of\r\n              low sample size or a program issue?</span></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\">\r\n    Neither of your attempted fixes &quot;resampling at the level of\r\n    observations&quot; or changing number of bootstrap resamples, are likely\r\n    to solve the low sample size issue.  You note there are 18 cardinal\r\n    sighting in your second stratum (not really sufficient to fit a\r\n    detection function).  When resampling, it is almost certain that\r\n    this number of sightings will be reduced (via resampling) such that\r\n    there may be very low (or no) sighting in the stratum.  I would\r\n    expect there to be a host of error messages that come from that\r\n    situation.</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><br>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n        <div>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">3. My &quot;p&quot;,\r\n              probability of\r\n              detections are concernedly low for conspicuous<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">forest birds, my\r\n              advisor says that\r\n              they are typically at 0.8/0.9 but I&#39;m<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">seeing 0.2/0.3.\r\n              Does this mean the modeling\r\n              seems to be invalid, or is<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">this just\r\n              reflecting the reality of\r\n              the sample? Note that there is an<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">interesting\r\n              potential difference in\r\n              observer &quot;p&quot; between treatments<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">because of the\r\n              highway noise, but it\r\n              doesn&#39;t show up as significantly<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n          <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt;font-family:&#39;Courier New&#39;;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">different for ETTI\r\n              or NOCA sets in\r\n              most analyses.</span></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\">\r\n    The definitive answer to this question requires careful study of the\r\n    data and the model results.  I don&#39;t know if your study used point\r\n    or line transects; for the sake of argument, I&#39;ll assume lines.  My\r\n    suspicion, given the values of estimated detection probability you\r\n    report, is that you have fitted a spiked detection function that\r\n    falls off very rapidly, leading to small values of p-hat.  Is the\r\n    shape of your fitted detection function plausible?  Again in a\r\n    hypothetical line transect, is it reasonable for your study that\r\n    your detection function is near 1.0 on the transect line, but falls\r\n    rapidly to ~0.3 at 5m (you miss 2 of 3 birds at 5m from the\r\n    transect, which would be the case with a spiked detection function)?<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    If that situation is not plausible, then your data may be\r\n    insufficient to support reasonable modelling.  Modelling and model\r\n    selection is not a black-box; it requires judgement regarding\r\n    plausible and implausible shapes for the detection function.<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    Hope that is helpful.<br>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
